run tests from tests folder with :
XDEBUG_MODE=coverage ../vendor/bin/phpunit --coverage-html ../public/coverage

or

../vendor/bin/phpunit --filter=<text>


db migrations with doctrine/migrations
(connection comes from the container, same EntityManager as bin/doctrine - no separate db config):

status / list:
php bin/doctrine-migrations migrations:status
php bin/doctrine-migrations migrations:list

create a blank migration:
php bin/doctrine-migrations migrations:generate

generate one by diffing the ORM mappings against the live schema:
php bin/doctrine-migrations migrations:diff

run everything pending:
php bin/doctrine-migrations migrations:migrate

preview the SQL without touching the database:
php bin/doctrine-migrations migrations:migrate --dry-run

roll back to a specific version:
php bin/doctrine-migrations migrations:migrate 20260405170003

one-off cutover for a database that was already migrated by Phinx - records the ported
migrations as executed WITHOUT running them, so they are not applied a second time:
php bin/doctrine-migrations migrations:sync-metadata-storage
php bin/doctrine-migrations migrations:version --add --all --no-interaction
(then the old `migrations_log` table can be dropped)

php bin/doctrine orm:schema-tool:update --force --dump-sql

php bin/doctrine orm:validate-schema

php bin/doctrine orm:clear-cache:metadata
php bin/doctrine orm:clear-cache:query
php bin/doctrine orm:clear-cache:result
